1304	  /**
1305	   * Returns a map with the given {@code values}, indexed by keys derived from those values. In
1306	   * other words, each input value produces an entry in the map whose key is the result of applying
1307	   * {@code keyFunction} to that value. These entries appear in the same order as the input values.
1308	   * Example usage:
1309	   *
1310	   * {@snippet :
1311	   * Color red = new Color("red", 255, 0, 0);
1312	   * ...
1313	   * ImmutableSet<Color> allColors = ImmutableSet.of(red, green, blue);
1314	   *
1315	   * ImmutableMap<String, Color> colorForName = uniqueIndex(allColors, c -> c.toString());
1316	   * assertThat(colorForName).containsEntry("red", red);
1317	   * }
1318	   *
1319	   * <p>If your index may associate multiple values with each key, use {@link
1320	   * Multimaps#index(Iterable, Function) Multimaps.index}.
1321	   *
1322	   * <p><b>Note:</b> on Java 8+, it is usually better to use streams. For example:
1323	   *
1324	   * {@snippet :
1325	   * import static com.google.common.collect.ImmutableMap.toImmutableMap;
1326	   * ...
1327	   * ImmutableMap<String, Color> colorForName =
1328	   *     allColors.stream().collect(toImmutableMap(c -> c.toString(), c -> c));
1329	   * }
1330	   *
1331	   * <p>Streams provide a more standard and flexible API and the lambdas make it clear what the keys
1332	   * and values in the map are.
1333	   *
1334	   * @param values the values to use when constructing the {@code Map}
1335	   * @param keyFunction the function used to produce the key for each value
1336	   * @return a map mapping the result of evaluating the function {@code keyFunction} on each value
1337	   *     in the input collection to that value
1338	   * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code keyFunction} produces the same key for more than one
1339	   *     value in the input collection
1340	   * @throws NullPointerException if any element of {@code values} is {@code null}, or if {@code
1341	   *     keyFunction} produces {@code null} for any value
1342	   */
1343	  @CanIgnoreReturnValue
1344	  public static <K, V> ImmutableMap<K, V> uniqueIndex(
1345	      Iterable<V> values, Function<? super V, K> keyFunction) {
1346	    // We can provide a hint to the builder to preallocate the correct size when the iterable is
1347	    // either a List (which likely has a fast size() implementation), or an ImmutableCollection
1348	    // (which definitely has a fast size() implementation). While Collection also has a size()
1349	    // implementation, it _may_ require iteration over the entire collection (e.g., a
1350	    // FilteredCollection), which we want to avoid.
1351	    if (values instanceof List || values instanceof ImmutableCollection) {
1352	      return uniqueIndex(
1353	          values.iterator(),
1354	          keyFunction,
1355	          ImmutableMap.builderWithExpectedSize(((Collection<?>) values).size()));
1356	    }
1357	    return uniqueIndex(values.iterator(), keyFunction);
1358	  }
